* ee-assist example: a 10 V resistive divider (DC operating point)
* SPICE suffix gotcha: `m` is milli and `MEG` is mega (a factor of 1e9 apart);
* ee-core's own netlist spells mega `M`, so this importer parses SPICE itself.
* The first line is always the title (SPICE tradition); node 0 is ground.
V1 in 0 DC 10
R1 in out 1k
R2 out 0 1k
.op
.end
